-- target: branch
--
-- LEVEL THE REHEARSAL BRANCH'S CLIENT-CALLABLE DOOR REGISTRY AND FEATURE KNOBS
-- WITH PRODUCTION'S.
--
-- WHY
-- ---
-- Two registries decide what the campaign's rehearsal is actually rehearsing:
--
--   `platform.client_callable_door` says which SECURITY DEFINER function a client role
--   may hold EXECUTE on at all — the branch's own `ddl_guard` reads it and takes a client
--   grant back the moment it is not declared. A branch whose door registry differs from
--   production's rehearses a different access surface, and its grants will not stick.
--
--   `platform.feature_knob` is every organization-configurable behaviour on the platform.
--   The branch carried TEN rows, all of them this campaign's own guards; production carries
--   769. Every knob read on the branch therefore fell back to a default the real system has
--   already moved off, and no lane could rehearse a knob-gated path honestly.
--
-- MEASURED 2026-09-17, production SELECT-only inside `begin transaction read only`.
--
-- THE DOOR REGISTRY — compared by (schema_name, function_name, identity_args TEXT), never
-- by OID
--   production 1,016 rows · branch 1,015
--   branch-only:     1 — `custom.record_write(...)`, this campaign's own write door. KEPT.
--   production-only: 2 — `seo._tm_live_topic_id(...)` and `seo._tm_remove_topics(...)`.
--                        NOT INSERTED — a NAMED EXCEPTION, refused by the branch's own live
--                        trigger `door_identity_is_the_catalogs()` (DD-223, SQLSTATE 23514):
--                        "a door row is a stand-down for the §6d-4 guard, so it may only name
--                        a function that exists", and neither function exists on the branch
--                        because `seo` is a feature schema whose drift is not this lane's.
--                        Levelling these two rows means levelling the `seo` SCHEMA first.
--                        The guard is correct and is not routed around, disabled, or
--                        weakened to make a count reach zero.
--   shared rows whose non-key columns differ: 25
--        `identity_argtypes` 19 — per-database type OIDs for the SAME type names. NOT drift,
--                                 NOT touched. This is exactly why the comparison key is the
--                                 identity-args TEXT.
--        `reason`             6 — production's text is newer (the seo ROUND 22 clauses).
--                                 FOUR are levelled below. The other two —
--                                 `seo.list_page_intents` and `seo.set_page_intents` — are
--                                 among the branch's ten orphan rows, so the SAME DD-223
--                                 trigger refuses an UPDATE to them. Named, not worked
--                                 around.
--
-- DOOR ROWS NAMING NO LIVE FUNCTION — the census, and why this file does not "clean" them
--   branch 10 · production 1. Nine of the ten branch orphans are `seo.*` and `public.*` door
--   rows that production ALSO holds and whose FUNCTION is simply absent from the branch —
--   `seo` is a feature schema outside platform/iam/history and its schema drift is not this
--   lane's to fix (it is `pnpm check:branch-schema-drift`'s subject). Deleting those rows
--   would move the branch AWAY from production, which is the opposite of the job. The tenth,
--   `web.create_site(... p_visibility visibility ...)`, is orphaned on PRODUCTION too: the
--   live function's identity args read `p_visibility platform.visibility` on both databases,
--   so the door row matches neither. That is a production defect this file records rather
--   than hides, and it is why one production grant (EXECUTE on `web.create_site` to
--   `authenticated`) cannot be levelled onto the branch: the branch's live `ddl_guard`
--   revokes it again the moment it is granted, correctly, because no door declares it.
--   A guard is never turned off to make a number go to zero.
--
-- THE KNOBS — configuration, never customer data
--   production 769 · branch 10 (all `feature = 'custom'`, this campaign's, all OFF).
--   COPIED: the 755 rows whose feature is not `custom`. The campaign's own knobs are NOT
--   touched, so every guard this campaign added stays exactly as its lane left it, and the
--   four `custom` rows production has and the branch does not stay absent — a lane's guard
--   is its lane's to land, never this file's to import.
--   NO SECRET COLUMN: the table is (feature, key, value, default_value, value_type, unit,
--   min/max, allowed_values, label, description, set_by, basis, review_due, updated_by,
--   overridable_by, override_direction, bound_value, ui, taxonomy_node_id, propagation,
--   public_read). Every production row was scanned for secret-shaped content (sk-, secret,
--   token, password, api key, bearer, an email address, a JWT); the 44 hits are all the
--   WORDS inside prose — "risk-", "kiosk", "token budget" — and no row carries a credential.
--   Nothing is synthesized because nothing needed to be.
--   `updated_by` IS DELIBERATELY NOT COPIED (3 rows carry one). It is a real person's user
--   id, it has no foreign key, and provenance of who last turned a production knob is not a
--   fact a rehearsal branch needs. It lands NULL.
--   `taxonomy_node_id` IS copied: all 67 nodes production's knobs reference exist on the
--   branch (checked, 0 missing), so the FK to `platform.taxonomy_node` holds.
--   `created_at` / `updated_at` take this database's `now()`, as a copy should.
--
-- BRANCH ONLY. `-- target: branch`, in `migrations/rehearsal/`, the directory no release
-- path scans. Production is the ANSWER here and never the subject.


-- ==========================================================================
-- DOOR — the two rows production has and the branch does not: NOT INSERTED, and why
-- ==========================================================================


-- ==========================================================================
-- DOOR — the four reachable shared rows whose `reason` production has moved on
-- ==========================================================================

update platform.client_callable_door set reason = 'WRITE. Records which topics a page covers, for one source. p_page_id -> platform admin or iam.has_access(''web_site'', page.site_id, ''editor''), decided before existence; the map is resolved through seo.site_map_id. p_topics -> a JSON array; [] clears this source''s coverage on purpose. p_source -> mapper | human | agent. NULL RULES: p_page_id=22023; p_topics=22023; p_source=22023 | FOREIGN: p_page_id=42501; p_topics=SAME; p_source=NONE | ROUND 22: a coverage target must be a LIVE topic; a retired or rejected slug comes back in `unknown_slugs`, byte-identical to an invented one.' where schema_name = 'seo' and function_name = 'set_page_map_topics' and identity_args = 'p_page_id uuid, p_topics jsonb, p_source text';
update platform.client_callable_door set reason = 'WRITE. Re-parents one topic. p_map_id -> seo._tm_map(editor). p_slug and p_new_parent_slug -> resolved only inside that map. NULL RULES: p_map_id=22023; p_slug=22023; p_new_parent_slug=MEANS move the topic to the root of the map | FOREIGN: p_map_id=42501; p_slug=P0002; p_new_parent_slug=P0002 | ROUND 22: p_new_parent_slug must name a LIVE topic — moving a live branch under a hidden parent hides the whole branch. Hidden and invented are the same P0002.' where schema_name = 'seo' and function_name = 'move_map_topic' and identity_args = 'p_map_id uuid, p_slug text, p_new_parent_slug text';
update platform.client_callable_door set reason = 'WRITE. Merges topics and moves their attachments. p_map_id -> seo._tm_map(editor). p_from_slugs, p_into_slug -> resolved only inside that map. Every bulk statement is scoped to the map''s organization_id; attachments filed under another organization are left alone and never reported. NULL RULES: p_map_id=22023; p_from_slugs=22023; p_into_slug=22023 | FOREIGN: p_map_id=42501; p_from_slugs=P0002; p_into_slug=P0002 | ROUND 22: p_into_slug must name a LIVE topic — merging into a hidden one buries every attachment it moves. Hidden and invented are the same P0002.' where schema_name = 'seo' and function_name = 'merge_map_topics' and identity_args = 'p_map_id uuid, p_from_slugs text[], p_into_slug text';
update platform.client_callable_door set reason = 'READ. Map health report. p_map_id -> seo._tm_map(viewer), access before existence. p_site_id -> one access-checked site, or NULL for the sites related to this map that pass iam.has_access(''web_site'', id, ''viewer'') (seo._tm_visible_sites); every page list, count and sites_using_map entry is restricted to that set. p_limit -> clamped to 1..200. NULL RULES: p_map_id=22023; p_site_id=MEANS the sites related to the map that the caller may view; p_limit=DEFAULT 25 | FOREIGN: p_map_id=42501; p_site_id=42501; p_limit=NONE | ROUND 22: `pages_on_no_topic` and its sample mean no `covers` edge into a LIVE topic OF THIS MAP. Before this, ANY seo_map_topic edge of any status and any map counted as coverage, so a page whose only topic had just been rejected — or whose topic belonged to another brand''s map — read as covered and never appeared in this number.' where schema_name = 'seo' and function_name = 'map_diagnostics' and identity_args = 'p_map_id uuid, p_site_id uuid, p_limit integer';

-- ==========================================================================
-- KNOBS — production's 755 non-campaign rows
